CHAPTER.VERS:
With kings and counsellors of the earth, which built 

          He notes the ambition of them who for their pleasure as it were change the order of nature, and build in most barren places, because they would by this make their names immortal.
         desolate places for themselves;

Wherefore is light given to him that is in misery, and 

          He shows that the benefits of God are not comfortable, unless the heart is joyful, and the conscience quieted.
         life unto the bitter [in] soul;

I was not in safety, neither had I rest, neither was I quiet; 

          The fear of troubles that would ensue, caused my prosperity to seem to me as nothing, and yet I am not exempted from trouble.
         yet trouble came.
